No note outlives what plays it: a track's clips end the notes they no longer play (Segno).

MIDI clips play through MidiNode, which keeps no record of the notes it started, and the
CombiningNode only ends notes of LoopingMidiNodes that vanish from a rebuilt graph. Instrument
plugins survive rebuilds without a reset, so any change to a track's MIDI while it plays (a clip
moved to another track, moved, trimmed or deleted; a sounding note deleted, transposed or
shortened; takes switched; undo) left the instrument holding the note until the playhead jumped.

- CombiningNode follows the notes its clips start and end, and takes the list over from its
  predecessor (by track) when the graph is rebuilt. The new graph's first block ends every listed
  note the clips don't play at the playhead any more; a note still played is left alone. A jump
  clears the list (PluginNode sends all-notes-off then); stopping ends what's held.
- MidiNode::addNotesPlayingAt gives the notes a clip plays at a moment, nothing while muted or
  when it's about to chase them (its note-ons come just after the note-offs).
- TimedNode::nodes() gives the nodes without copying them (getNodes() allocates).

To upstream (tracktion_engine develop).

